ot control. It prevents you from being blown off your hand by a raise and ensures you see the river card. If the river is safe (a blank), you can still extract value from a King. If the opponent has a monster, you minimize your losses. Given there are 12 hands left and the chip deficit is small, playing solidly to realize your equity is preferable to over-committing on a wet board.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
